# Pending human-applied patch — issue #427, PR #565
#
# WHAT: adds an actions/setup-python step to the CI `test` job, so
#       `pythonAvailable()` in engine/src/guard/guard.fuzz.test.ts returns non-null on
#       the runner and the two differential safety-parity tests actually execute there.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS: docs/PLAN.md's M1 Verification section states the guard port is proven
#       by a differential fuzz against the predecessor project's guard.py (1500 seeded commands, 0
#       divergences on the shared surface). PR #565 vendored guard.py as an in-repo
#       fixture, which removed the `existsSync(GUARD_PY)` half of the skip condition.
#       This patch removes the other half. Until it lands, the two tests still skip in
#       CI on `pythonAvailable()` alone — expected, and called out in #427's
#       "Human-owned remainder".
#
# WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT: .github/workflows/** is human-merge-only
#       (docs/security.md "Human-merge-only paths"), enforced by the guard, not by
#       convention. An autonomous worker's write is denied at the tool level — verified
#       while producing this patch:
#         BLOCK [write-path] .github/workflows/** (CI integrity) is human-merge-only
#       The guard constrains Claude tool calls, never a human's editor.
#
# APPLY (from the repo root), then delete this file:
#       git apply docs/patches/427-ci-setup-python.patch
#       git rm docs/patches/427-ci-setup-python.patch
#
# NOTE ON NECESSITY: the GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest image does ship a system python3,
#       so the tests may already run without this step. That is a runner-image detail
#       which can change without notice, and this repo's own CI has no assertion that
#       would notice if it did — the tests would simply go back to skipping silently,
#       which is precisely the failure mode #427 exists to close. The explicit step
#       pins the interpreter and makes the guarantee deterministic. guard.py imports
#       only the stdlib (os, re, shlex, dataclasses, collections.abc) — no pip step.
#
# Generated against .github/workflows/ci.yml at blob 3ca2c512 (post-image 5b8dff7e).
# If the file has since moved, the hunk still locates by context (offset-tolerant);
# re-check the result.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 3ca2c51250d50c3591212640c5a9e2c83f4286cd..5b8dff7e351c547dd24940f226868085b4ed84d6 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -13,6 +13,13 @@ jobs:
           node-version: 24
           cache: npm
           cache-dependency-path: package-lock.json
+      # guard.fuzz.test.ts runs the vendored guard.py snapshot
+      # (engine/src/guard/fixtures/guard_py_snapshot/) through this interpreter for the M1
+      # safety-parity differential. Without an interpreter both differential tests t.skip() —
+      # that is the half of the #427 gap the fixture alone could not close. Stdlib only.
+      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
+        with:
+          python-version: "3.12"
       - run: npm ci
       - run: npm --workspace engine run typecheck
       - run: npm --workspace dashboard run typecheck
